WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:09.650
Finding out that our enemies were in fact the descendants of humans banished to Jupiter

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.050
seems to have been a shock for most everyone here.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.710
Meanwhile, some people are getting closer, some people farther away.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.590
A lot sure happens on this ship.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.190
With the Y Unit,

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:57.500
the Nadesico has four phase transition engines,

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.890
making her an invincible battleship.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.870
Or so we would like to say,

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:04.240
but actually things aren't so good as we're really pushing it.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:09.310
A "Reunion That Came Too Late"

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.900
So right now,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.310
we're on route to a rendezvous with the mobile dock ship Cosmos.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.690
What about this for a slogan?

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:20.140
Don't mess with battleship module docking; dorky docking docks you.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:23.770
What?

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.650
Where is everyone?

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.100
A notice came in from the main office, so everyone from Nergal is going over the budget.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.880
Everyone else is getting counseling from Inez-san.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.590
Counseling?

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.510
I understand that everyone's feelings are wavering.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.430
Because they found out that our enemies were humans just like us?

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.610
Our enemy was the mysterious force known as the Jovian Lizards.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.930
We fought on thinking that, but then...

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.360
Most likely that's what's going through their minds.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.230
I understand how they feel, but...

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.930
If everyone is feeling like that, then a pilot like Akito,

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.530
my dear lovely Akito, must be really, really,

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.290
REALLY depressed.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.320
And I'm the only one that can help!

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.460
Yes, that's it! That must be the case!

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.210
Ruri-chan, take care of everything for me, please.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:13.730
DASH!

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.220
Will she ever learn?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.910
I'm a soldier.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.930
So it doesn't matter that the enemy are humans.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.140
I won't reject the war based on that.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.220
But I have to admit I feel deceived by the military as well.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.920
I understand how you feel.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:29.940
Akito?

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.480
Where are you, Akito?

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:32.650
Yurika!

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.810
Are you there, Akito?

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.380
See?

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.400
I understand how you feel.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.370
That's why men are so worthless in the end.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.570
When things turn against you...

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:44.790
Akito, where are you?

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.780
Minato-san, what are you going to talk about?

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.250
I think that it's important to feel wanted by someone.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.330
Back when I was a voice actress, I always said that to myself as I stood in front of the microphone.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.180
What?! You were a voice actress before, Megumi-san?

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.390
Akito, answer me.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.080
What?! You were a voice actress before, Megumi-san?

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.180
You were a voice actress, Megumi-san?

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.190
Akito...!

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:07.630
Yes.
Akito...!

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:08.170
Akito...!

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.020
Akito?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.180
You're a pilot fighting on the front lines, inside an Aestivalis.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:14.200
I can see how you feel.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:14.940
Pilot? I found Akito!
I can see how you feel.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.330
Pilot? I found Akito!

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.860
Captain's orders! Get out of the way!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:22.610
What?

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.280
You're the owner of a firm heart, Doctor.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:29.700
I'm... It's because I'm preoccupied with finding something.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.290
Nobody needs to doctor the doctor.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.190
Okay, next person.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.330
Captain, what is it?

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.110
Has Akito visited you?

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.220
If it's Akito-kun.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.050
He's with Ryoko-chan.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.780
And they're all alone.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:50.740
Why? Why?

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:52.600
Captain!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.350
Wonderful timing. We need to talk.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.590
Could you bring this up later? Right now, I'm...

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.570
We have a major issue at hand.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.170
Well, you see...

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.660
What's wrong, you two? You're all sullen.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.840
What's the point of getting neurotic now?

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.900
I'm out of here.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.350
We come in, pumped up about this being a righteous battle,

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:24.490
only to find out that this is like any other stinking war.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.690
What a joke.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:27.850
Still...

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.810
I've decided that I have to fight this war.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.730
Guess you're a lot stronger than I figured at first.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.200
No one's ever said that to me before.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.190
You're strong, believe it.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:40.610
Hikaru-chan!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.390
Yes, Uripee?

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.450
Embezzlement by Uribatake-san?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.870
That seems to be the only logical explanation.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.090
We know how he is, so we have been rather lenient

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.610
with his accounting irregularities, as they imply costs

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.790
attributable to the various mysterious devices he builds,

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.480
but this time... See?

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:56.580
Ack!

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.710
Isn't it?

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.910
As I understand it, there is a rumor that he's become

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:03.610
very familiar with a certain female crewperson on this ship.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:04.590
It's Amano Hikaru.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:11.010
In any case, we believe an investigation is in order here.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.030
Yes. The Admiral seems to be caught up in some discussions

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:17.440
with headquarters. Why don't we take care of this on our own?

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:22.720
A wise decision. If the Admiral ever finds out, we most certainly would not hear the end of it.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:23.810
That is all.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.820
But that's... that's unfair.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.200
Papa...

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:38.290
So how come I get dragged into this stuff about embezzlement?

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:40.730
Because if it does have something to do with romantic relationships,

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.300
then I have no idea how to deal with it.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.880
I don't understand how men think, except for you, Akito.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.540
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.340
But Hikaru-chan?

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.810
That's kind of hard to believe.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.030
You're right.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.810
It's not like a destined encounter happens every day.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.400
You and I are truly special.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.150
That's about enough.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.230
Oh, that's wonderful.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.260
Pretty cool, isn't it?

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.650
It really is. I never realized you were so adept.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:06.840
Can I try too?

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.050
Sure, how you hold it makes all the difference.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:11.540
Like this?

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.980
You need to be more gentle with it.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.280
That's it. Oh, yeah, now you've got it.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.330
What the hell are you up to?

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.300
Hello.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.760
Wow, it sure is realistic!

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.280
Isn't it? I was really impressed,

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.680
so I'm having Uripee teach me how to build models.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.360
See, it's a Sailor Valis!

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.050
So you weren't getting intimate or anything, I guess.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:38.520
1 /35th?

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:39.710
1 /48th.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.680
Here, I'll get one for you to keep.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:43.110
Really?

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.130
Oh, yeah!

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.050
The world of models is the eternal romantic realm of men.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:51.200
For these are not mere toys, but a true hobby for adults.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.120
What are you doing?

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.210
What? Well, I was just adding bullet holes to it.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.040
Now I just file off the edges a little bit here.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.580
Now, isn't that realistic?

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.500
Yes, very realistic, but...

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.590
So, Captain, did you have some business with us?

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:14.810
Oh, that's right!

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:18.240
Uribatake-san, I assume that the money you misappropriated

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.670
didn't go toward models.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.980
The accounting irregularities have reached a level

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.440
that makes you say "ack!"

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.020
Ack!

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.940
You wouldn't mind telling me where the money went to, would you?

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.630
Wow!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.780
The money went into this?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.920
I've been working on this little by little for quite a while now.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.840
An Uribatake original model,

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:37.580
I've named it the X-Aestivalis.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.460
X-Valis for short!

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.270
X-Aestivalis!

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.920
X-Valis for short!

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.350
That's right.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.760
Equipped with an advanced generator that I customized,

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:52.190
its gravitron wave conversion efficiency has increased five-fold.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.280
A juggernaut with the mobility of the standard Aestivalis

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:57.730
and the power of the lunar surface frame.

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:00.840
With this baby, you'll match up against Jupiter's giant robots!

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:03.850
But...

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.650
But?

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.950
I thought we were fighting lizards.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:09.310
I can't bring myself to work on something that kills other people.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.570
That's it! This is it!

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:12.530
This will work just fine!

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.760
As admiral I'm ordering you!

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.950
I want you to complete this new weapon, as soon as possible!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.410
What is this about?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.490
I've just been notified that I might be demoted soon.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:25.820
At this rate, I might have my position as admiral taken away.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:29.500
Just because you found out about the true identity of the enemy.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.780
But I won't have it!

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.340
I have no intention of being made to suffer because of you morons!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.450
But with this Aestiva-X...

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.900
X-Valis!

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.350
In any case, I'll make the top brass recognize my value once more

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:44.270
with the advanced abilities of this new weapon!

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:47.940
So, you're saying you're going to use my X-Valis as a tool to safeguard your position?

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:49.600
I won't accept no as an answer!

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.840
I'll do whatever it takes to keep myself on top!

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:55.360
That's how I do things!

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.290
This is a direct order!

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:00.070
You will finish this new weapon at once!

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.020
You got that?!

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.170
Do whatever it takes to stay on top?

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:09.590
Then does that mean it was him?

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.930
Reversal of Fortune! Gekigan Nunchaku!

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:22.810
So, I see.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.640
Tenkawa is drawing the line at last.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.200
Kung Fu movies are so cool.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:29.880
Oh, just look at you, Junpei!

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.650
Would you mind turning off that annoying manga?

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:32.830
It really irks me to have to listen to that main character's lines.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:36.490
Yeah, but listen carefully. Even if you are pretending,

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:36.770
don't do your Kung Fu moves on other people.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.040
It's fine as it is.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:38.500
don't do your Kung Fu moves on other people.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.580
Can't you follow my instructions?

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:43.410
Who's going to pilot your X-Valis?

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.090
Okay, everyone, let's have some ramen and then go home.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:45.950
So, what do you want?

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:46.830
Just what I wanted!

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:47.290
It's about the death of the person who loved this Gekiganger 3 series.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:51.040
Oh God, this is too much, this can't be!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:51.750
Yamada Jirou.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:54.170
Soul name, Daigoji Gai!

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:54.500
Daigoji Gai.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:55.830
Ken, your master has been murdered!

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.770
Murdered? My master's been murdered?!

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:08.110
Saigou Jigai?

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.790
That's right. I killed your master.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:11.760
What?!

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:14.220
Stronger ones win.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:14.680
Who's that?

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:15.820
That is the way of...

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.310
Wait, I'll remember soon.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.650
Well... I...

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:22.050
This is true righteousness!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.250
Oh, about that.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:32.660
I am a mecha monster from Kyo'Ak, Dragon Fighter L!

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.170
Damn it.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:34.710
You're still worried about that? You need to move on.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:35.740
I'll make you pay.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:36.230
You're still worried about that? You need to move on.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.790
Let's go, Joe, Akira! Time for Gekiganger!

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.100
It was just as it was reported.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.460
He was shot in self-defense.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:41.880
I'll show you what real righteousness is!
He was shot in self-defense.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:42.360
I'll show you what real righteousness is!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.680
Are you sure about that?

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:43.950
Let's...

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.010
No question about it.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:45.310
Is that the truth?

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:46.120
Gekiga-In!

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:46.880
That's the truth.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.070
The truth...

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.310
How it hurts to be denied knowing the truth.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.650
You should know how that feels right now, Admiral.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:56.650
Please tell me, Admiral! Why did Gai have to die?!

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:03.670
I have nothing more to say. There is only one truth.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.000
And the standoff ends.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.600
Houmei-san, do you have any tea strainers you can let go?

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.420
Tea strainers? What do you want them for?

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.210
Part of building Uripee's diorama.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:22.650
Oh, this is fun!

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.010
I want to make it snow here too.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.540
Baking soda makes really convincing snow for dioramas.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.180
The crystals reflect the shimmering light...

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:41.600
What's up?

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:44.530
Hikaru-chan,

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.570
well, I... you see...

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.450
Hey, you!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.990
A ghost?!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.280
What are you doing, enthralled with models?!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.780
What about my Aestiva-X?!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.070
It's done!

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:55.380
Really?

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:56.790
But...

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:57.920
But what?

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.960
A failure?

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.540
Didn't I tell you?

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.780
There are problems with its energy amplification systems.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:08.700
The feedback from the generators,

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.870
reflecting increased gravitron wave conversion efficiency,

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.690
has gotten really bad. The unit can't handle the stress.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.020
I wanted it to have show-stopping armament, an X-Cannon.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.580
So I gave it a gravity blast cannon,

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.330
but if one were to actually charge the gun with enough energy to fire,

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:23.250
it'd probably blow up.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:27.280
Oh, well. Don't get on my case about something that I started working on as a hobby.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.500
Guess you'll just have to give up.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.890
I won't hear of it!

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.970
The Aestiva-X is my last hope!

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:37.570
I'm at the cliff's edge! I'm at the end of my rope!

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:41.480
Don't you dare say you'll give up just like that!

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:42.010
STOP!

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.180
You should be ashamed of yourself, Admiral.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.350
An officer should conduct himself as befits his position.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:53.080
...tai kono jiyuu to kagayaki wo

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:54.960
sora to umi to daiji to minna no PAWAA

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:57.560
I'm sorry, but we need to close shop pretty soon.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:58.230
hitori ga minna no tame ni

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.900
There was a time, once...

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.630
Yes?
hitori ga minna no tame ni

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:01.050
A time when I believed in justice and righteousness.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.250
yuuki wo dashite saa tachi agarouze!

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:04.280
A time when I believed in justice and righteousness.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:07.700
"RETTSU GEKIGAIN!"

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.240
I have to take a break.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:30.010
Don't people tell you that you look cute with your glasses off?

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.930
Oh, come on, we're not in a romance comedy from last century.

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:39.240
These days no one would dare use that, even as a doujin plot.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.500
What are you saying, Uripee?

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.320
I'm jealous, Hikaru-chan.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:49.530
If I had met a girl like you long ago, I'd probably be a really happy man.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:52.830
Me? You've got to be kidding.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.630
Don't say that.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.470
Someone that understands my hobbies,

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.240
being with someone who I can spend time having fun with,

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:02.470
someone who gets the same jokes and references.

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:04.090
I've dreamed about that for a long time.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.090
It's much more fun if your tastes are the same.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:07.510
You think so?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:12.430
I'm sure Uripee's lover would be a very happy person.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:13.610
You think so?

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:18.350
Hikaru-chan, can I talk about something with you?

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.110
To tell you the truth, Hikaru, you mean to me...

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:21.770
Why don't we stop?

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.940
I wanted to be close to you without having that come between us.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:30.570
People misunderstand me all the time, especially my friends.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.670
That's not what I had in mind.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:37.500
Because isn't all of this different from love and relationships?

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.420
I suppose so.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.950
Hobbies and love affairs are separate.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:45.180
I only realized that after I moved out on my ex-boyfriend.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:47.870
Hikaru-chan, you've lived with a man before?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.050
I suppose... Yeah, it makes sense.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.680
Hikaru-chan's a modern girl, after all.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:58.390
I'm sorry, Uripee.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.870
I'll make this the last time I come here.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.050
Identification signal confirmed. It's the Cosmos.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:29.140
Confirm rendezvous point.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:30.970
All mechanics, please prepare for docking.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:35.770
It's the enemy.

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:37.180
Enemy?

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.210
Time to launch the Aestiva-X!

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:39.850
Admiral?!

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.020
Let's Gekiga-in!

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.980
Our dreams call out for tomorrow,

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.460
Listen to our soul yell out,

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.490
Let's go, passion!

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.010
Some day peace will come,

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:54.950
With these hands we will reclaim it!

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:57.290
Admiral! Admiral Munetake!

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:58.330
Please come in.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:58.840
Admiral Munetake!

00:16:58.840 --> 00:16:59.510
Here I go!

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.290
Behold, cursed Jovian Lizards who threaten the Earth!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.530
We have to do something, or the Cosmos is going be in big trouble.

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:08.030
But what?

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:09.800
Can't we just shoot him down?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.800
We've been instructed to get him into safe custody.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:12.750
Why?

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:14.560
Why is he doing something like this?

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:20.090
There is no question of the existence of true righteousness!

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:22.980
Neither shall the corrupting forces of evil be dismissed!

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.230
Feel the might of true righteousness!

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.750
Is he serious?!

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:29.390
Now what?

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.860
Guess we'll have to forcibly drag him back!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.150
Too late! Get away!

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.490
Once he starts charging up energy, it's too late.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:41.800
Unless I stop them here, Tokyo will be in ruins!

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:44.420
Hold on! Hold on, Aestiva-X!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:50.780
Gekiganger!

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.900
There's a friend of justice at your side!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.260
That voice!

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.230
Yes! No longer do I have to deny my transient name,

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.180
for now I truly am Daigoji Gai!

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:00.510
Behold my presence!

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.430
After all that, you'll help me?

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.350
An ally of righteousness doesn't hold grudges from the past.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.770
Come on, be brave and together we'll preserve true righteousness!

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:11.110
Gai...

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.230
I've managed to get an audio link to him.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.500
Patch him through!

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:15.990
Thank you, Gai.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:18.870
What? What did he just say?!

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:19.950
Now, let's do it!

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:27.500
Gekigan Flare!

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:53.360
It always hurts to be betrayed by what you believe in.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.820
Are you talking about the Admiral?

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:58.550
Well, yeah, but that goes for all of us too, right?

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.360
The war for peace turns out to be just another war.

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:08.960
It's harsh.

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:10.400
Yeah.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.880
There, it's all done.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.850
Wow, it sure is realistic.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:22.100
Yes, but they are only models, after all. Not real war.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:26.100
I've been in love with killing machines for dozens of years.

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:29.520
I'd like to think I've learned to balance realism and reality.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.110
That's pretty mature.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:35.540
I told you. Model building is a mature hobby.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.070
Hey, wait! That Aesti is...

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.920
I wanted to make it his Aestivalis.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:47.480
I see. But "Gai" wasn't written anywhere on his Aesti.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:49.270
It..., it wasn't?

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:50.720
It happens all the time.

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:52.540
You think you have this precious memory,

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.440
but you don't realize that you've actually been rewriting it.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.850
Well, that's probably not such a bad thing, either.

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:58.630
Uribatake-san!

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:01.080
This has been bothering me for a while now,

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:03.050
but this definitely is not realistic.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.770
Ruri-chan does not have such a killer body,

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:09.410
and I have bigger breasts then this.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:11.400
You would know, Akito, right?

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:14.070
Hey, watch it! People will get the wrong idea about us!

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.810
In any case, please do another one for me.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.020
This time make my arms much slimmer, and...

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:27.330
YOU!

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:30.300
What the hell are you doing with my model?!

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:30.950
I'm so sorry!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.140
God may forgive you, but I certainly won't!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.230
Akito, help me!

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:38.260
Stop dragging me into things!

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:40.320
All yours.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:48.410
Hello, everybody!

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:51.700
I'm the little magical girl princess from the kingdom of magic,

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:53.340
Natural Lychee!

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:56.040
So, so, what will you become when you grow up?

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:59.390
I want to marry a doctor or a lawyer and... oops.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:02.620
But wouldn't it be terrible if you found out that you were a princess?

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:04.380
Oh, I'd really rather not, really.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:07.960
Anyway, the next episode will be
"Echoes of Self, Echoes of Water".

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.280
Lychee, Lycheru, Lycheolla, Lychee!

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:11.360
Baka.
